  "pending": [
    "The machine holds 96 patterns in three groups and two banks. The engine holds 32, so here there are two pattern groups of sixteen and no banks: the third PATTERN key and the BANK keys are not on the panel.",
    "Four tracks of up to 192 measures each, where the machine has eight sharing 896. A track plays the patterns of one group: the one chosen with the PATTERN keys while it is written.",
    "A step is on or off. The two strengths of a note and flam are not here: loudness is the total accent row and the level knobs, each instrument's pair of keys is one instrument, and SHUFFLE has no FLAM side.",
    "On the machine the open hi-hat is keys 13 and 14 together. Here key 13 is the closed hi-hat and key 14 the open one.",
    "SHIFT, INSTRUMENT SELECT, LAST STEP, SHUFFLE and CLEAR are latches: press one, then the key it works on. On the machine they are held down. Esc lets them up.",
    "STOP stops, and there is no CONTINUE: the engine starts a pattern or a track from its beginning.",
    "A chain of patterns is chosen with SHIFT and the key at its other end, where the machine has you hold the first key and press the last. The engine is given a chain when it starts, so choosing one while the machine runs stops it. CYCLE is read when a track starts.",
    "In pattern write the step keys choose the pattern while the machine is stopped and write it while it runs. CLEAR then a key clears that pattern when stopped and that key's instrument when running; in track write CLEAR empties the track at once. How the machine itself clears is from general descriptions, not checked on one.",
    "The tempo runs from 40 to 290, where the machine's starts at 37. The seven shuffle settings are spread evenly up to half a step late; how far the machine's go was not measured.",
    "EXT INST, TEMPO MODE, TAPE SYNC, GUIDE, the cartridge and the step keys' track-editing functions (numbers, COPY, INS, DEL) are not on the panel. A track is edited with BACK, FWD, ENTER and LAST MEAS.",
    "The voices are synthesised, the hats and cymbals too, where the machine plays recordings of them. What each knob does to the sound, and how far the level, accent and volume knobs reach, is a model made from descriptions. Nobody has listened to it yet.",
    "What the lamps and the display show in each mode follows general descriptions of the machine and is unverified against one."
  ]
